# Build-context ignore for deploy/Dockerfile only (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next
# to the Dockerfile), so it cannot change today's Nixpacks build. Every pattern here is a file git
# never tracks: Railway and CI build from git, where none of these exist. It guards a local
# `docker build` from copying a checkout's dependencies, build output or secrets into the image,
# where the final `COPY . /app` would overwrite the freshly built client bundle and Linux modules.
**/node_modules
client/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
.tmp
coverage
.git
